  [1mThe main design choice:[0m the repo has a vendored Keel kit ([38;5;153mvendor/kit/[39m) that already covers everything the page needs:
  - [1m[38;5;153mpageHeader[0m for the title and snapshot time.
  - [1m[38;5;153mfilterBar[39m + [38;5;153mselectField[0m for the environment dropdown. It keeps the current sort, and [38;5;153mkit.js[39m reloads the page when
    the selection changes.
  - [1m[38;5;153mdataTable[0m for the table. Its sortable headers work exactly like the Services page's hand-written ones (clicking the
    active column flips it, [38;5;153maria-sort[39m, ▲/▼).
  - [1m[38;5;153mbadge[0m for the status chips. Its tones line up with the spec's colors: ok is green, bad red, warn amber, info blue.
  - [1m[38;5;153memptyState[0m for "No deploys in staging".

  So the page is one module that puts these together. It doesn't copy the markup from [38;5;153mservices.js[39m, and it needs no new
  CSS.

  [1mThe two tasks:[0m
  1. [1m[38;5;153msrc/pages/deploys.js[0m: [38;5;153mrenderDeploys[39m and [38;5;153mformatDuration[39m, plus 10 rendering tests. They cover the filter, both sorts,
     the chips, the duration format, the empty state and the fallback for unknown query values.
  2. [1mWiring it up[0m: the [38;5;153m/deploys[39m route in [38;5;153mserver.js[39m, the "Deploys" nav link after "Services", a README line, and server
     tests. Those check the route, where the link sits in the nav, and the 503 for both a missing file and a
     half-written one.

  [1mDecisions the spec left open[0m (listed at the top of the plan, worth a look):
  - An unknown [38;5;153mdir[39m falls back to [38;5;153mdesc[39m, because the default view is newest first.
  - Deploys of the same service stay newest first when you sort by Service.
  - The subtitle reads "Snapshot from <raw timestamp>".
  - With "All environments" selected and nothing to show, the page says "No deploys".
  - Durations under a minute keep the minutes, e.g. "0m 45s".

